The codebase contained 6 unbounded recursive functions and loops that could cause stack overflow errors on pathological inputs (deeply nested directories, malformed HTML, or many duplicate names).

## Changes

### Recursive functions with depth limits
- **RecursiveFolderCopy.CopyTo**: Added 100-level depth limit for directory copying
- **NotesParser.goThrowNodes**: Added 500-level depth limit for HTML traversal
- **fileManagerClasses.getUniqueName**: Added 1000-recursion limit with timestamp fallback
- **fileManagerClasses.RenameTopic**: Added 1000-recursion limit with timestamp fallback

### Loops with iteration limits
- **NotesParser.ParentTextNode**: Added 1000-iteration limit with null checks on parent traversal
- **NotesParser.addHeading**: Added 100-iteration limit with null checks on heading hierarchy traversal

## Example

Before:
```csharp
void goThrowNodes(HtmlNode node)
{
    foreach (HtmlNode child in node.ChildNodes)
    {
        onNode(child, ref areInHeading, ref currentHeadingAnswer);
    }
}
```

After:
```csharp
void goThrowNodes(HtmlNode node)
{
    goThrowNodes(node, 0);
}

private void goThrowNodes(HtmlNode node, int depth)
{
    if (depth > 500) return; // Prevent stack overflow

    foreach (HtmlNode child in node.ChildNodes)
    {
        onNode(child, ref areInHeading, ref currentHeadingAnswer, depth);
    }
}
```

